  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Sorting, Paging, Index Use",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Pair sort with limit",
          "text": "`$sort` followed by `$limit` keeps only the top-N in a bounded heap instead of sorting everything. Moving `$limit` next to `$sort` is the highest-leverage rewrite you own."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Paging",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "$skip 100000",
                "lines": [
                  "walks 100000 docs",
                  "O(skip)",
                  "degrades linearly"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "range paging",
                "lines": [
                  "$match on last id",
                  "index seek",
                  "O(limit)"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "[{$match:{_id:{$gt:lastSeenId}}},",
            " {$sort:{_id:1}},",
            " {$limit:20}]   // constant cost per page"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "MongoDB's sort is not stable for equal keys",
            "Add `_id` as a tiebreaker for deterministic paging",
            "Range key should be indexed and near-unique"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "ESR And Direction",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Compound index serving `$match` plus `$sort`: Equality, Sort, Range",
            "Getting S and R backwards forces an in-memory sort",
            "Sort direction must match the index or be its exact reverse on all keys",
            "Mixed directions need a matching mixed-direction index",
            "Collation differences make an index unusable for the sort"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Windows Over Rows",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$setWindowFields` (5.0+): running totals, ranks, moving averages",
            "Spec is `partitionBy`, `sortBy` and an output window",
            "No self-join needed for any of it",
            "`$densify` (5.1) and `$fill` (5.3) close time-series gaps first"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Arrays sort oddly",
          "items": [
            "Ascending sorts by the array's minimum element",
            "Descending sorts by its maximum element",
            "Never by the array as a whole"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Golden Order",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "$match",
              "$project",
              "$lookup",
              "$unwind",
              "$group",
              "$sort+$limit"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$match` first, as selective as possible — the only index gate",
            "`$project`/`$unset` early, before a blocking stage buffers docs",
            "`$limit` as early as correctness allows, above `$lookup`/`$unwind`",
            "`$unwind` as late as legal — every later stage sees the multiplied stream",
            "Every deviation from this order should be deliberate"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Order, Optimizer and explain()",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What The Planner Does",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Rewrite",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "$match coalescing",
              "adjacent merge"
            ],
            [
              "$sort + $limit",
              "top-N heap"
            ],
            [
              "$limit + $limit",
              "smaller wins"
            ],
            [
              "$skip + $limit",
              "swapped"
            ],
            [
              "$match pushdown",
              "before $unwind"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The line it will not cross",
          "text": "It never pushes a `$match` past a `$group` on a field the group invented — that reordering would change results."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading explain",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.aggregate(p, { explain: true })",
            "db.c.explain('executionStats')",
            "  .aggregate(p)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Signal",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "IXSCAN",
              "index used"
            ],
            [
              "COLLSCAN",
              "full scan"
            ],
            [
              "SORT stage",
              "blocking sort"
            ],
            [
              "examined 1000:1",
              "no index on $match"
            ],
            [
              "examined = returned",
              "healthy"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The `$cursor` entry shows the find() derived from your leading stages",
            "That derived find() is the only part indexes apply to",
            "`executionTimeMillisEstimate` per stage names the bottleneck",
            "Read it; do not guess which stage is slow"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Spill, Hint, Fan-Out",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`allowDiskUse: true` spills blocking stages to `_tmp`",
            "It turns an error into a slow query, far slower than fitting in memory",
            "`aggregate(p, { hint: 'idx_name' })` forces an index when the planner picks badly",
            "`$facet` runs several sub-pipelines over the same input in one pass",
            "Only stages BEFORE `$facet` can use an index"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Writing results out",
          "items": [
            "`$out` replaces the target collection wholesale",
            "`$merge` upserts incrementally into it",
            "Basis for materialized views and on-demand rollups"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Misplaced Stages",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Wrong",
            "Repair"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "$match after $group",
              "split predicate, raw fields first"
            ],
            [
              "$unwind before $match",
              "filter, then fan out"
            ],
            [
              "$sort with no $limit",
              "pair for top-N heap"
            ],
            [
              "$limit below $lookup",
              "hoist it above"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Filter raw stored fields early, derived fields late",
            "Every doc unwound then discarded is pure waste",
            "A wide `$project` of all fields costs BSON serialization for nothing"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Errors That Cost Real Latency",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Join Errors",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No index on `foreignField`: COLLSCAN inside the lookup plan",
            "Latency then scales with the foreign collection size",
            "`createIndex` on the foreign key is the whole fix",
            "ObjectId versus string key gives silently empty results"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.items.createIndex({ sku: 1 })",
            "// or normalize the key type:",
            "{ $match: { $expr: { $eq: [",
            "  '$_id', { $toObjectId: '$$cid' } ] } } }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Array Errors",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$unwind` without `preserveNullAndEmptyArrays` deletes empty-array docs",
            "`$push` on a high-cardinality group throws 'BSONObjectTooLarge'",
            "Push only the fields you need, or use `$topN`",
            "`$unwind` plus `$group` where `$reduce` would do it in place"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $addFields: { total: { $sum:",
            "  { $map: { input: '$items', as: 'i',",
            "    in: { $multiply:",
            "      ['$$i.qty','$$i.price'] } } } } } }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Index Defeats",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$expr` in a leading `$match` — denormalize the compared value instead",
            "Unanchored `$regex`; only left-anchored `/^abc/` uses an index prefix",
            "`$skip`-based deep pagination — range-page on an indexed sort key",
            "`allowDiskUse` papering over an unindexed pipeline",
            "Assuming `$group` preserves order — it does not"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Cache the query, not the pain",
          "text": "Running the same expensive aggregation per request? `$merge` into a rollup collection on a schedule and serve reads from that."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Pipeline is slow. Where do you look, in order?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`totalDocsExamined` versus `nReturned` first",
            "Then whether a blocking SORT stage appeared",
            "Then inside `$lookup` for a COLLSCAN",
            "Only then start rewriting stages"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "db.c.explain('executionStats')",
            "  .aggregate(pipeline)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
